<div id=3D"outline-container-org551a211" class=3D"outline-3">
<h3 id=3D"org551a211">Simon Cruanes announced</h3>
<div class=3D"outline-text-3" id=3D"text-org551a211">
<p>
Howdy, I just released moonpool 0.12, now coming to an opam repository near=
 you.
</p>

<p>
Moonpool (first announced <a href=3D"https://discuss.ocaml.org/t/ann-moonpo=
ol-0-1/12387">here</a>) is a threadpool library for OCaml 5, leveraging dom=
ains to actually go brrrrrrr on multiple cores. The (still unique=E2=80=BD)=
 design of moonpool allows the user to create multiple pools, whose cumulat=
ive size exceeds <code>Domain.recommended_domain_count()</code> without slo=
wdown. It does that by using=E2=80=A6 threads=E2=80=A6 instead of domains. =
Yep.
</p>

<p>
Anyway there's a whole bunch of bugfixes (including one to correct patholog=
ical memory usage in #45, big up @gasche as usual :heart_hands:), support f=
or <code>ambient-context</code>, some cleanup, dscheck for tests, etc.
</p>

<p>
Cheerios on you and your cereal bowls
</p>
