<div id=3D"outline-container-orgf10ffc5" class=3D"outline-3">
<h3 id=3D"orgf10ffc5">Thibaut Mattio announced</h3>
<div class=3D"outline-text-3" id=3D"text-orgf10ffc5">
<p>
Hi everyone!
</p>

<p>
I'm happy to announce the release of <a href=3D"https://github.com/invarian=
t-hq/windtrap">Windtrap</a>, a testing framework for OCaml that brings the =
different testing methods of the ecosystem into one library:
</p>

<ul class=3D"org-ul">
<li>Unit tests, with an Alcotest-like API.</li>
<li>Expect and snapshot tests, with a companion PPX compatible with <code>p=
px_expect</code> and <code>ppx_inline_test</code>, but usable without it.</=
li>
<li>Property tests as seen in <a href=3D"https://github.com/c-cube/qcheck">=
QCheck</a>, with a library of textbook laws (round trips, orders, associati=
vity, and more).</li>
<li>Stateful and differential tests, as seen in <a href=3D"https://github.c=
om/ocaml-multicore/multicoretests">qcheck-stm</a> and <a href=3D"https://gi=
tlab.inria.fr/fpottier/monolith">Monolith</a>, on one domain or several.</l=
i>
<li>Test coverage (as with <a href=3D"https://github.com/aantron/bisect_ppx=
">Bisect_ppx</a>) and mutation testing (as with <a href=3D"https://github.c=
om/jmid/mutaml">mutaml</a>).</li>
</ul>

<p>
Every kind of test composes with the others into one suite and one output, =
and the library has <b>no dependencies</b> beyond OCaml (the optional PPX u=
ses ppxlib).
</p>

