<p>
We built Windtrap at <a href=3D"https://invarianthq.dev/">Invariant</a> as =
part of our work on making code written by agents more trustworthy. Agents =
replicate what they find in a repository, so a project full of strong tests=
 gets more of them. Windtrap comes with an <a href=3D"https://github.com/in=
variant-hq/windtrap/blob/main/SKILL.md">agent skill</a> that guides agents =
towards the right kind of test, but we care just as much about humans, and =
put a lot of effort into making the API and output ergonomic and delightful.
</p>

<p>
You can read more about it in the <a href=3D"https://invarianthq.dev/blog/a=
nnouncing-windtrap/">announcement post</a>. It walks through an example sui=
te, what a failure looks like, coverage and mutation testing, and an experi=
ment where we used Windtrap to test the OCaml standard library.
</p>

<p>
To install it (when <a href=3D"https://github.com/ocaml/opam-repository/pul=
l/30817">the PR</a> is merged on opam-repository):
</p>

<pre class=3D"example" id=3D"org5f94ce4">
opam install windtrap ppx_windtrap=20
</pre>

<p>
The <a href=3D"https://github.com/invariant-hq/windtrap/tree/main/doc/manua=
l">manual</a> (written by agents with my guidance, I hope you'll find the w=
riting voice bearable, but if enough people complain I'll look into rewriti=
ng it by hand) has one page per kind of test. Feedback is very welcome, her=
e or on the <a href=3D"https://github.com/invariant-hq/windtrap/issues">iss=
ue tracker</a>.
</p>

<p>
Happy hacking!
</p>

<p>
&mdash;
