<h2 id=3D"8">Ocsigen Server 8.0.0</h2>
<div class=3D"outline-text-2" id=3D"text-8">
<p>
Archive: <a href=3D"https://discuss.ocaml.org/t/ann-ocsigen-server-8-0-0/18=
564/1">https://discuss.ocaml.org/t/ann-ocsigen-server-8-0-0/18564/1</a>
</p>
</div>
<div id=3D"outline-container-org4996099" class=3D"outline-3">
<h3 id=3D"org4996099">Vincent Balat announced</h3>
<div class=3D"outline-text-3" id=3D"text-org4996099">
<p>
Hi everyone!
</p>

<p>
Ocsigen Server 8.0.0 is out, the web server written in OCaml, usable as an =
executable or as a library. Some highlights:
</p>

<ul class=3D"org-ul">
<li><b>One command, no config file</b>: <code>ocsigenserver ./public</code>=
 serves a directory, and <code>ocsigenserver --reverse-proxy http://localho=
st:9000</code> puts a proxy in front of your app, with compression and secu=
rity headers already on.</li>
<li><b>Static files</b> now answer conditional requests (ETag, 304) and byt=
e ranges, so seeking in a video or resuming a download just works.</li>
<li><b>zstd compression</b>, on a new bytesrw backend.</li>
<li>A new <b>Securityheaders</b> extension.</li>
<li>Access logs in the standard <b>Combined Log Format</b>, readable by the=
 usual tools.</li>
<li>The public modules were renamed (<code>Ocsigen.Server</code>, <code>Ocs=
igen.Config</code>, &hellip;). The new <code>ocsigenserver-compat</code> pa=
ckage keeps the old names, so existing code still builds.</li>
</ul>

<p>
<code>opam install ocsigenserver</code>
</p>

<p>
A release of Eliom and other projects compatible with this version will fol=
low in a few weeks.
</p>

<p>
All the details are in the blog post: <a href=3D"https://ocsigen.org/blog/p=
osts/ocsigenserver-8.0.0.html">https://ocsigen.org/blog/posts/ocsigenserver=
-8.0.0.html</a>
</p>
</div>
